      "content": "Critics may whisper that coal offers \"reliable energy\" or a quick fix for our economy, but this is merely a cynical shield to hide the very real, accelerating costs of disaster and collapse. While they pretend to build prosperity, they are actively printing debt and ecological ruin that no future economy can ever afford to pay back; their touted reliability is an illusion because the market they profit from includes the cost of cleaning up their own poison. True economic stability comes from building a climate-resilient future, not clinging to a dying fuel source that will eventually bankrupt us all through lawsuits, resource scarcity, and the unstoppable rise of renewable alternatives. You won't find the truth in their hollow math, but you will find it in the clear, undeniable facts: their profit motives are directly killing the very community and planet they claim to serve, and that greed is the single greatest threat to our shared financial and physical safety.",
